From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:25:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] drm/amd/display: the Dolby Vision tunnel through a
 passive DP++ adaptor that says HDMI

The tunnel and its properties were on HDMI connectors only. A
DisplayPort connector with a passive dual-mode adaptor (DP++) that
identifies itself as an HDMI one, to an HDMI display, carries HDMI that
DC sends itself (amdgpu_dm_dual_mode_of()): the Dolby vendor InfoFrame
and the AVI InfoFrame of the tunnel go through it as on an HDMI
connector, and the bytes of the scanout are the same. What the adaptor
limits is the TMDS clock, which DC keeps every stream within
(DC_EXCEED_DONGLE_CAP): the tunnel is RGB at 8 bits, so 1080p at 24 to
60 Hz goes through either type, 2160p at 24 to 30 Hz (297 MHz) through a
type 2 adaptor of 300 MHz, and 2160p50 or 60 (594 MHz) through none.

A DisplayPort connector of a single stream now has the properties of the
tunnel where an HDMI connector has them (DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB, its
Low-Latency, HDMI 1.4b and HDR forms, DVBRIDGE_REFUSED), and
DVBRIDGE_DUAL_MODE, read only, which says after each look at the display
what is behind it: "none" (a DisplayPort display, an active converter,
or no display), "HDMI adaptor", or "other adaptor" (a DVI one, one
without the HDMI signature, or a DVI display). The connector check
(amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_tmds_hdmi()) takes the tunnel on such a connector
only through an HDMI adaptor; anything else is refused as before, as
"converter", with what is behind the port in the kernel log. A mode that
the adaptor does not carry in RGB at 8 bits is validated by DC in YCbCr,
and the scanout check refuses that for what it is (the TMDS clock, or
4:2:0), with the clock of the adaptor in the log. The HDR10 depth guard
and its answer stay on HDMI connectors. An HDMI connector is as before,
and a DisplayPort connector without an adaptor refuses the tunnel as it
always did; user space (Kodi) asks for it only where DVBRIDGE_DUAL_MODE
says "HDMI adaptor".

Checked: KUnit of amdgpu_dm (x86_64 in QEMU), with the test patch of
this series: the links that carry the tunnel, for 11 connectors and
adaptors, and the TMDS clock of each type for the modes of the tunnel;
W=1 of the four objects without warnings.

Not tried with an adaptor on hardware.
